---
import StoryHero from './StoryHero.astro';
import StoryChapter from './StoryChapter.astro';
import ComposerBrandStudies from './ComposerBrandStudies.astro';
import ComposerInteractionGallery from './ComposerInteractionGallery.astro';
import type { WorkEntry } from '../../data/work';
interface Props { work: WorkEntry }
const { work } = Astro.props;
---
<composer-case>
  <StoryHero
    title={'Could a library\nshape a brand\nexperience?'}
    intro="Buzzvil already knew how to reach people likely to be interested. I built the Interaction Composer to explore the next question: how could we turn that knowledge into a different brand experience for each audience?"
    links={[{ label: 'Read the original research', url: '/blog/a-design-system-for-an-agent/' }]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="visual"><ComposerBrandStudies variant="cover" /></Fragment>
  </StoryHero>

  <StoryChapter id="composer-challenge" scope="The design challenge" title={'Knowing whom to reach\nwas only half the problem.'} intro="From 2025, Buzzvil’s focus expanded beyond getting a campaign seen or clicked. Our targeting and retargeting, including reaching people who had already shown interest, gave us a strong starting point. The next challenge was to shape what those people experienced with the brand.">
    <figure class="composition-brief">
      <div class="brief-inputs">
        <div><span>Who is this for?</span><h3>Audience context</h3><p>What we know about a group’s interests and behavior, informed by Buzzvil’s data and analysis.</p></div>
        <div><span>What should it feel like?</span><h3>Brand context</h3><p>The brand’s identity, product information and insights, so the interaction belongs to that brand.</p></div>
        <div><span>What should it achieve?</span><h3>The advertiser’s goal</h3><p>The action the campaign aims to encourage, such as a purchase. This is its key performance indicator, or KPI.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="brief-composition"><span>Interaction Composer</span><p>Choose and combine interactions<br/>for this audience, brand and goal.</p></div>
      <div class="brief-outputs"><span>A tailored journey for each audience group</span><div><span>Discover the brand</span><span>Explore the product</span><span>Take the next step</span></div></div>
      <figcaption>A possible journey, composed from audience and brand context.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="challenge-decision"><h3>Personalize the journey<br/>through the campaign.</h3><p>A user segment is a group of people with shared characteristics. The design challenge was to turn what we knew about each group into a relevant sequence of interactions, while keeping the brand recognizable and the advertiser’s goal clear. One generic landing page could not express all of those differences.</p></div>
  </StoryChapter>

  <StoryChapter
    id="composer-library"
    scope="My proposed approach"
    title={'One library could assemble\ndozens of interactions.'}
    intro="My proposal was to give the AI a library of interaction patterns it could combine using audience data, brand context and the advertiser’s goal. Alongside the product team’s research, I built the Composer and a testing tool, the UI Cooker, to assemble and compare those variations."
    class="library-scene"
  >
    <ComposerInteractionGallery />
    <div class="recipe-caption">
      <details class="code-note">
        <summary>Inside the recipe</summary>
        <pre aria-label="Original coupon component manifest excerpt"><code>{`id: 'CouponCard',
intent: 'reward',
flowPredecessors: ['FlipCard', 'ScratchReveal', 'SpinWheel'],
compositionRules: [{
  role: 'reward',
  constraints:
    'Use as the reward reveal after a discovery interaction. ' +
    'Always pair with a CTA so users can act on the coupon.'
}]`}</code></pre>
        <p>Original manifest excerpt. Each component carried design intent: where it belonged, how it behaved and what came next. Recipes combined these parts into flows.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </StoryChapter>

  <StoryChapter
    id="composer-test"
    scope="Zoom in · One campaign refinement"
    title={'Real campaigns revealed\nsmall reasons to leave.'}
    intro="Generating a flow was only the first test: people also had to stay with it. The Composer ran in a few campaigns, where usage data drove dozens of refinements. Here is one focused example, addressing people leaving before reaching the product."
    class="reward-scene"
  >
    <div class="reward-board">
      <div class="reward-thinking">
        <h3>Keep the reward<br/> within reach.</h3>
        <p class="reward-context">I kept the reward visible throughout the quiz, so every answer would show progress toward a clear payoff. Compare the two versions, then try the three questions.</p>
        <div class="detail-switch" role="group" aria-label="Compare reward visibility">
          <button type="button" data-reward-mode="before" aria-pressed="false">Before</button>
          <button type="button" data-reward-mode="revised" aria-pressed="true">Revised</button>
        </div>
        <div class="reward-annotation" aria-live="polite">
          <p data-reward-note>The reward stays in sight. Every answer makes progress tangible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reward-device-area">
        <div class="phone-frame">
          <div class="device-cap" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><b></b></div>
          <div class="reward-phone" data-reward-mode="revised">
            <div class="reward-brand"><strong>FORME</strong><span>Your daily ritual</span></div>
            <div class="reward-photo"><img src="/work/composer/forme-campaign-768.webp" alt="FORME Daily Wash bottles on a stone ledge" width="768" height="512" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span>Good habits.<br/>Less waste.</span></div>
            <div class="reward-body">
              <div class="reward-progress">
                <div class="reward-progress-label"><span>Your discovery reward</span><span data-answer-count>0 / 3</span></div>
                <div class="gauge-track" role="progressbar" aria-label="Discovery reward progress" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="3" aria-valuenow="0"><i></i></div>
              </div>
              <div class="quiz-content">
                <span class="question-kicker" data-question-number>Discover / 01</span>
                <h3 id="reward-question" data-question>A fresh start needs a new bottle.</h3>
                <div class="reward-choices" role="group" aria-labelledby="reward-question"><button type="button" data-answer="O"><span aria-hidden="true">O</span>True</button><button type="button" data-answer="X"><span aria-hidden="true">X</span>False</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="complete-content" hidden>
                <span class="question-kicker">Discovery complete</span>
                <h3 tabindex="-1">A little care,<br/>on us.</h3>
                <p>Your reward is ready.<br/>Explore the Daily Wash.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="answer-feedback" data-answer-feedback>Three small discoveries. One daily essential.</p><span class="sr-only" data-quiz-status role="status"></span>
              <button type="button" class="reset-quiz" data-reset>Start again</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="device-home" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="figure-note">Reconstructed refinement from campaign feedback. Its effect on conversion remains unconfirmed.</p>
  </StoryChapter>

  <StoryChapter
    id="composer-pivot"
    scope="Back to the research question"
    title={'We chose richer context\nover a larger UI kit.'}
    intro="Alongside my Composer experiments, the product team tested instructions and supporting tools for the AI, without restricting it to a library of interface components. Results were stronger and more flexible. Generating and validating an experience for each audience group on the server made the extra generation time acceptable."
    class="pivot-scene"
  >
    <figure class="review-figure" id="composer-delivery">
      <div class="review-workspace story-artifact">
        <div class="workspace-bar"><span>Experience studio <i>/</i> FIELDWORK</span><span class="workspace-status" data-workspace-status>Draft · human review</span></div>
        <div class="workspace-content">
          <aside class="brand-context" aria-label="Illustrative brand context for generation">
            <span class="panel-label">01 / Generation context</span>
            <div class="brand-wordmark">FIELD<br/>WORK</div>
            <div class="brand-swatches" aria-label="Charcoal, chalk and acid yellow palette"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <div class="guideline"><span>Brand</span><p>Equipment for life outside.</p></div>
            <div class="guideline"><span>Example audience</span><p>New visitors</p></div>
            <div class="guideline"><span>Example advertiser goal</span><p>Product purchase</p></div>
            <div class="guideline"><span>Design guidance</span><p>Utility. Real texture.<br/>A clear next step.</p></div>
            <p class="context-source">Prompts + research tools<br/>+ design guidelines</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="review-canvas">
            <div class="canvas-toolbar"><span class="panel-label">02 / Compose & review</span><div class="variant-controls" role="group" aria-label="Preview illustrative campaign versions"><button type="button" data-variant="story" aria-pressed="true">Brand story</button><button type="button" data-variant="product" aria-pressed="false">Product first</button></div></div>
            <div class="campaign-preview" data-variant="story">
              <div class="preview-header"><strong>FIELDWORK</strong><span>Collection 03 / Everyday equipment</span></div>
              <div class="preview-body">
                <img src="/work/composer/fieldwork-campaign.webp" srcset="/work/composer/fieldwork-campaign-768.webp 768w, /work/composer/fieldwork-campaign.webp 1536w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 92vw, 700px" alt="A charcoal FIELDWORK shell, photographed against concrete architecture" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                <div class="preview-story"><span>No destination required.</span><h3>TAKE THE<br/>LONG WAY.</h3></div>
                <div class="preview-product"><span>Everyday equipment / 01</span><h3>THE<br/>STUDIO<br/>SHELL.</h3><p>One layer.<br/>No set route.</p></div>
                <span class="preview-index">FW-03</span>
              </div>
              <div class="preview-footer"><span data-variant-copy>From the first train to the last light.</span><span class="preview-cta" aria-hidden="true">Discover the collection</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="review-decision"><div><span class="panel-label">03 / Human decision</span><p data-review-copy>Judge the experience before anyone sees it.</p></div><button type="button" data-approve aria-pressed="false">Approve this version</button></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="server-branch"><div><span class="branch-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>04 / Server branch</span></div><p data-branch-status>Awaiting review <span>Audience: new visitors</span></p></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Concept demonstration with a fictional brand. Compare versions, then approve one to try the review flow.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="decision-caption">
      <div><h3>The Composer favored speed.</h3><p>Shared components worked well for the possibility of live generation: a new experience for each session.</p></div>
      <div><h3>The chosen flow favored quality.</h3><p>Brand-research tools and design guidance gave the model more freedom. Admin-side generation gave us time to review each variation.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="closing-note">The campaign platform serves a validated interaction to each user segment. If a segment underperforms, we can generate and validate another version on the server. Generation time stays outside the user’s experience.</p>
  </StoryChapter>

  <StoryChapter
    id="composer-learnings"
    title={'What I learned: better context,\nless machinery.'}
    class="learning-scene"
  >
    <div class="learning-grid">
      <article class="learning-item">
        <div class="learning-visual library-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="learning-stage">01 / UI library</span>
          <div class="kit-pieces">
            <span class="kit-wide"><i></i><i></i></span><span class="kit-disc"><i></i></span>
            <span class="kit-pair"><i></i><i></i></span><span class="kit-lines"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="kit-disc"><i></i></span>
            <span class="kit-lines"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="kit-wide"><i></i><i></i></span>
          </div>
          <span class="learning-visual-note">Compose from what exists</span>
        </div>
        <h3>A library has a ceiling.</h3>
        <p>Our UI kit made generation fast, but limited the quality and range of the results. Matching the model’s freedom would mean a much larger library and a growing system to maintain. The reason to build it became less convincing.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="learning-item">
        <div class="learning-visual harness-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="learning-stage">02 / Context + tools</span>
          <div class="harness-layers"><div><div class="learning-inputs"><span>Brand</span><span>User data</span><span>Goal</span><span>Prompt</span></div></div></div>
          <span class="learning-visual-note">Give the model room to compose</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Context mattered more.</h3>
        <p>Brand details, user data and the advertiser’s goal proved more valuable inputs than a catalog of components. A clear prompt connected them. Richer context gave the model room to produce stronger experiences, which we validated before delivery.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="learning-item">
        <div class="learning-visual minimal-visual" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="learning-stage">03 / Where we are going</span>
          <div class="learning-inputs"><span>Brand</span><span>User data</span><span>Goal</span><span>Prompt</span></div>
          <span class="learning-visual-note">Keep the inputs. Reduce the layers.</span>
        </div>
        <h3>The AI needs less scaffolding.</h3>
        <p>As models improve, we’re gradually removing layers that earlier models needed. What remains is the essential context: user data, the brand, the goal and a clear prompt connecting those factors to the goal.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="learning-footnote">The direction, simplified. The prompt logic remains proprietary; human validation still happens before delivery.</p>
  </StoryChapter>

</composer-case>
<script>
class ComposerCase extends HTMLElement {
 connectedCallback() {
  if(this.dataset.ready) return;
  this.dataset.ready='true';
  const questions=[
   {text:'A fresh start needs a new bottle.',O:'Not always. Keep the bottle; refill the ritual.',X:'Exactly. Keep the bottle; refill the ritual.'},
   {text:'A simple routine can be a daily ritual.',O:'Exactly. Small habits deserve a little care.',X:'Even a small habit can become a ritual.'},
   {text:'An everyday essential should earn its place.',O:'Exactly. Fewer things, chosen well.',X:'Choose what works for your everyday.'}
  ];
  let answers=0;
  const phone=this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.reward-phone')!;
  const progress=this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.gauge-track')!;
  const quiz=this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.quiz-content')!;
  const complete=this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.complete-content')!;
  const feedback=this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-answer-feedback]')!;
  const updateQuiz=()=>{
   progress.setAttribute('aria-valuenow',String(answers));
   progress.querySelector<HTMLElement>('i')!.style.width=`${answers/3*100}%`;
   this.querySelector('[data-answer-count]')!.textContent=`${answers} / 3`;
   phone.classList.toggle('complete',answers===3);
   quiz.hidden=answers===3;complete.hidden=answers!==3;
   if(answers<3){
    this.querySelector('[data-question]')!.textContent=questions[answers].text;
    this.querySelector('[data-question-number]')!.textContent=`Discover / 0${answers+1}`;
   }
  };
  this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-answer]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   if(answers>=3)return;
   const response=questions[answers][button.dataset.answer as 'O'|'X'];
   answers++;updateQuiz();
   feedback.textContent=response;
   this.querySelector('[data-quiz-status]')!.textContent=answers<3?`${response} ${answers} of 3 complete. ${questions[answers].text}`:`${response} Discovery complete. Your reward is ready.`;
   if(answers===3)complete.querySelector<HTMLElement>('h3')!.focus({preventScroll:true});
  }));
  phone.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   answers=0;updateQuiz();feedback.textContent='Three small discoveries. One daily essential.';
   this.querySelector('[data-quiz-status]')!.textContent='Discovery restarted. '+questions[0].text;
   this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-answer]')!.focus({preventScroll:true});
  });
  this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reward-mode]').forEach(button=>{
   if(button.tagName!=='BUTTON')return;
   button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
    phone.dataset.rewardMode=button.dataset.rewardMode;
    this.querySelectorAll('button[data-reward-mode]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));
    this.querySelector('[data-reward-note]')!.textContent=button.dataset.rewardMode==='before'?'The reward appeared at the end. During the quiz, the payoff was out of sight.':'The reward stays in sight. Every answer makes progress tangible.';
   });
  });
  const approval=this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-approve]')!;
  const workspace=this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.review-workspace')!;
  const setApproval=(approved:boolean)=>{
   approval.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(approved));
   approval.textContent=approved?'Reopen for review':'Approve this version';
   workspace.classList.toggle('approved',approved);
   this.querySelector('[data-workspace-status]')!.textContent=approved?'Reviewed · ready to assign':'Draft · human review';
   this.querySelector('[data-review-copy]')!.textContent=approved?'Reviewed. This version can become a server branch.':'Judge the experience before anyone sees it.';
   const branch=this.querySelector('[data-branch-status]')!;
   branch.firstChild!.textContent=approved?'Reviewed version ready ':'Awaiting review ';
  };
  approval.addEventListener('click',()=>setApproval(approval.getAttribute('aria-pressed')!=='true'));
  this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-variant]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   if(button.getAttribute('aria-pressed')==='true')return;
   this.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.campaign-preview')!.dataset.variant=button.dataset.variant;
   this.querySelectorAll('button[data-variant]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));
   this.querySelector('[data-variant-copy]')!.textContent=button.dataset.variant==='story'?'From the first train to the last light.':'The Studio Shell / Charcoal';
   setApproval(false);
  }));
  this.querySelector('[data-workspace-status]')!.setAttribute('role','status');
 }
}
if(!customElements.get('composer-case'))customElements.define('composer-case',ComposerCase);
</script>
<style>
.composition-brief { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--theme-border); }
.brief-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); }
.brief-inputs>div { padding: clamp(1.25rem,3vw,2.25rem); min-width: 0; }
.brief-inputs>div+div { border-left: 1px solid var(--theme-border); }
.brief-inputs span,.brief-composition>span,.brief-outputs>span { font: .75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.brief-inputs h3 { margin: 1.1rem 0 .8rem; font: 400 1.3rem/1.3 var(--font-body); }
.brief-inputs p { margin: 0; font: .9rem/1.7 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
.brief-composition { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--theme-border); text-align: center; background: color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-accent) 6%,var(--theme-bg)); }
.brief-composition p { margin: 1rem 0 0; font: 400 clamp(1.2rem,2.5vw,1.8rem)/1.45 var(--font-body); }
.brief-outputs { padding: 1.5rem; text-align: center; }
.brief-outputs>div { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
.brief-outputs>div>span { padding: .65rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--theme-border); border-radius: 4px; font: .85rem/1.5 var(--font-body); }
.composition-brief>figcaption { padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem; font: .75rem/1.6 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); text-align: center; }
.challenge-decision { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
.challenge-decision h3 { margin: 0; font: 400 clamp(1.4rem,2.5vw,2rem)/1.3 var(--font-body); }
.challenge-decision p { margin: 0; font: 1rem/1.8 var(--font-body); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
@media(max-width:650px) { .brief-inputs,.challenge-decision { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .brief-inputs>div+div { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--theme-border); } .challenge-decision { gap: 1rem; } }

/* StoryHero and StoryChapter own the editorial rhythm. Product studies keep their own UI. */
.recipe-caption{padding:1.5rem 0 0}
.recipe-caption .code-note{max-width:44rem}
.review-workspace.story-artifact{--line:var(--theme-border);--muted:var(--theme-text-muted);--soft:color-mix(in srgb,var(--theme-text) 4%,var(--theme-bg));color:var(--theme-text)}
/* Global typography belongs to the portfolio shell; product UI owns its contrast. */
:global(composer-case .reward-phone :where(div, p, span, h3, h4)), :global(composer-case .campaign-preview :where(div, p, span, h3, h4)) { color: inherit; }
.preview-body::after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(to top,rgba(32,34,32,.88),rgba(32,34,32,.3) 50%,transparent 80%);pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .4s}
.preview-story,.preview-product,.preview-index{z-index:1}
.preview-index{background:#f1f1e8;padding:.4em .5em}
